WO-03a · deploy.bash · Post-Reload Generator Validation
Problem: daemon-reload returns exit code 0 even when the Quadlet generator silently fails to produce a .service file for a specific unit. A successful deploy can leave the system in a broken state with no visible error.
Task: Immediately after every daemon-reload call, run an explicit validation step for the unit that was just deployed:

Check if the corresponding .service file exists in ~/.config/systemd/user/.
If it exists, compare its mtime against the .container file just written. If .container is newer, the generator ran but rejected this file.
On either failure condition, print a GEN_FAIL error with the instruction to check journalctl --user -xe for the Quadlet generator output. Do not report deploy success.
On pass, report success as normal.

This step must run before any downstream actions (container restart, status check).

